    {
      "title": "{{PROJECT}}: telemetry export failing",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "range",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 900,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasourceUid": "{{DATASOURCE}}",
          "model": {
            "editorMode": "code",
            "expr": "sum(count_over_time({app=\"{{ALLOY_APP}}\"} |~ \"Exporting failed|Partial success\" [15m]))",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "queryType": "range",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 900,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasourceUid": "__expr__",
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 900,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasourceUid": "__expr__",
          "model": {
            "conditions": [
              {
                "evaluator": {
                  "type": "gt",
                  "params": [
                    2
                  ]
                }
              }
            ],
            "expression": "B",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "OK",
      "execErrState": "Error",
      "for": "5m",
      "keep_firing_for": "0s",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "Alloy could not hand a batch to Grafana Cloud, either outright or in part. The partial case is the one that bit: the tenant's active series limit rejects some data points from an otherwise accepted request, and the app's own metrics ride the same batch, so a scrape that mints too many series starts costing app samples. Exporting failed alone missed it.",
        "summary": "{{PROJECT}}: telemetry export failing"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "warning"
      },
      "isPaused": false
    },
    {
      "title": "{{PROJECT}}: model failures",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "range",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 1800,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasourceUid": "{{DATASOURCE}}",
          "model": {
            "editorMode": "code",
            "expr": "sum(count_over_time({app=\"{{APP}}\"} | json | event=~\"llm[.](feedback|hardcore|chat)[.](formatter_unavailable|grader_unavailable|moves_unavailable|judge_unavailable|shout_unavailable|transport_error|no_json|schema_mismatch|empty_output|decision_drift|moves_mismatch|judge_mismatch|failed)\" [30m]))",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "queryType": "range",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 1800,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasourceUid": "__expr__",
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 1800,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasourceUid": "__expr__",
          "model": {
            "conditions": [
              {
                "evaluator": {
                  "type": "gt",
                  "params": [
                    1
                  ]
                }
              }
            ],
            "expression": "B",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "OK",
      "execErrState": "Error",
      "for": "5m",
      "keep_firing_for": "0s",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "The model failures that cost a user their chat turn, their feedback or their grade, over 30 minutes: a chat turn that died mid-stream, judge, grader, formatter and moves unavailable, transport errors, unparseable JSON, a response that did not match the schema, empty output, and a decision or move set that drifted from the transcript. Left out on purpose: no_material and empty_transcript are what a candidate hears when there was nothing to grade, and stub_deterministic is stub mode. Fires above 1 event. Read from the log lines and not from llm_outcome=\"error\": only the line names the stage that failed, and it counts a retried call once where the metric counted it twice.",
        "summary": "{{PROJECT}}: model failures"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "warning"
      },
      "isPaused": false
    },
    {
      "title": "{{PROJECT}}: outside dependency failing",
