      ],
      "noDataState": "OK",
      "execErrState": "Error",
      "for": "5m",
      "keep_firing_for": "0s",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "The two third parties the app cannot serve without: the speech-to-text provider, unreachable or rejecting the key, and Clerk, where a failed user lookup blocks sign-in. voice.quota_exhausted is left out because that is a candidate using up their own minutes, not a fault. Fires above 1 event in 30 minutes.",
        "summary": "{{PROJECT}}: outside dependency failing"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "warning"
      },
      "isPaused": false
    },
    {
      "title": "{{PROJECT}}: container near its memory limit",
      "condition": "C",
      "noDataState": "OK",
      "execErrState": "Error",
      "for": "10m",
      "keep_firing_for": "0s",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "A container in {{PROJECT}} has been sitting above its declared memory limit. Both numbers come from the kubelet, the working set and the cgroup's own limit, so this rule needs no second exporter and no join across sources. Containers with no declared limit divide by a value near the node's capacity and cannot fire.",
        "summary": "{{PROJECT}}: container near its memory limit"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "warning"
      },
      "isPaused": false,
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "range",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 600,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasourceUid": "{{DS_PROM}}",
          "model": {
            "editorMode": "code",
            "expr": "max by (namespace, pod, container) (container_memory_working_set_bytes{namespace=\"{{PROJECT}}\", container!=\"\"}) / max by (namespace, pod, container) (container_spec_memory_limit_bytes{namespace=\"{{PROJECT}}\", container!=\"\"})",
            "instant": false,
            "legendFormat": "working set / limit",
            "range": true,
            "refId": "A",
            "queryType": "range",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 600,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasourceUid": "__expr__",
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 600,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasourceUid": "__expr__",
          "model": {
            "conditions": [
              {
                "evaluator": {
                  "type": "gt",
                  "params": [
                    0.9
                  ]
                }
              }
            ],
            "expression": "B",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "{{PROJECT}}: container oom killed",
      "condition": "C",
      "noDataState": "OK",
      "execErrState": "Error",
      "for": "0s",
      "keep_firing_for": "0s",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "A container in {{PROJECT}} was killed by the kernel out-of-memory killer. On one replica that is an outage. This reads the cgroup's own OOM counter rather than a restart total, so it names the cause; a crash that is not an OOM is reported by the app's own absent(target_info) rule and by the uptime probe.",
        "summary": "{{PROJECT}}: container oom killed"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "critical"
      },
      "isPaused": false,
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "range",
